-- THE HOSTILE READING: the findings of NOTES.md section 4 that the encoding can show. Each
-- assertion states the answer the text gives on its words, which is the surprising one; a
-- satisfied assertion here is evidence of a defect in the instrument, not of a defect in
-- the encoding. Findings that are reading only are in NOTES.md and not here.

§ `Findings`

§§ `X1 — renewal: definition 36 against definition 38`

-- An employee insured since 1 January 2025, renewing on 1 January 2026, whose condition
-- first appeared and was known on 1 June 2025 (in the first year of cover), claims under
-- Benefit 4 in June 2026. Read with def 38 (fork F1) the condition arose during cover. Read
-- with def 36 alone ("the first day of EACH period of cover") it existed before the start
-- date and is pre-existing, so III.8 bars it every year after the year it appeared.
GIVETH AN `An event`
`a condition from June 2025` MEANS
    `an event built from` `an illness` (YMD 2026 6 1) TRUE FALSE `another illness or injury` (YMD 2025 6 1) NOTHING (JUST (YMD 2025 6 1)) NOTHING EMPTY NOTHING FALSE

#ASSERT NOT `a pre-existing condition, judged at` (`the start date for` (`the renewing employee, continuously` TRUE)) `for` `a condition from June 2025`
#ASSERT `a pre-existing condition, judged at` (`the start date under definition 36 alone for` (`the renewing employee, continuously` TRUE)) `for` `a condition from June 2025`
#ASSERT `the claim is covered` (`a claim under` `the plain contract` `by` (`the renewing employee, continuously` TRUE) `for` `a condition from June 2025` `on` `Benefit 4` `for` (`medical expenses` (`an inpatient stay from` (YMD 2026 6 1) `to` (YMD 2026 6 3)) EMPTY) `on` (YMD 2026 6 1))

§§ `X2 — the Annex covers illness, but its transport condition names only accidents`

GIVETH A `The transport`
`an evacuation` MEANS
    `The transport` WITH
        `service`                                              IS `emergency medical transport to the nearest suitable hospital`
        `cost, in US dollars`                                  IS 10000
        `consecutive days away from the declared residence`    IS 5
        `within Vietnam`                                       IS TRUE
        `in a critical condition`                              IS TRUE
        `the necessary treatment unavailable where the accident happened` IS TRUE
        `approved by PTI beforehand`                           IS TRUE
        `certified by the treating doctor as unavailable there` IS TRUE
        `transport costs already paid in the period, in US dollars` IS 0
        `the call`                                             IS (`A call to the assistance centre` WITH `name, policy number and expiry date given` IS TRUE, `telephone number and location given` IS TRUE, `short description of the condition given` IS TRUE, `hours from admission to notifying the assistance company` IS NOTHING, `the medical team allowed access to the insured` IS TRUE, `a reasonable excuse for not complying` IS FALSE)

-- For a stroke (an illness) the literal words of II.4 can never be met; fork F48 reads them
-- purposively, and Benefit 7 responds.
#ASSERT NOT `II.4 on its literal words allows transport for` `the plain contract` (`an illness from` (YMD 2026 3 1) `diagnosed as` `another illness or injury` `with` EMPTY) `an evacuation`
#ASSERT `II.4 on its literal words allows transport for` `the plain contract` (`an accident on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `with` EMPTY) `an evacuation`
#ASSERT `Benefit 7 responds to` `an evacuation`

§§ `X3 — two first-year rules for special and pre-existing disease`

-- Hepatitis first appearing on 10 January 2026, an employee in a group of 40, Benefit 4,
-- a stay on 1 August 2026. IV's second 32 table says 6 months for an employee in a group of
-- 30 or more, and the claim is covered (fork F11). III.8 says 365 days for special disease;
-- 212 days have run, so applied as well, it would bar the claim and leave the table nothing
-- to do.
GIVETH A `A claim`
`a hepatitis claim in a group of 40` MEANS
    `a claim under` (`a 2026 contract for` 40 `employees and` 40 `persons with` EMPTY) `by` `the employee`
        `for` (`an illness from` (YMD 2026 1 10) `diagnosed as` `hepatitis` `with` EMPTY) `on` `Benefit 4`
        `for` (`medical expenses` (`an inpatient stay from` (YMD 2026 8 1) `to` (YMD 2026 8 3)) EMPTY) `on` (YMD 2026 8 1)

#ASSERT `the claim is covered` `a hepatitis claim in a group of 40`
#ASSERT `days from the start date to the loss in` `a hepatitis claim in a group of 40` EQUALS 212
#ASSERT `days from the start date to the loss in` `a hepatitis claim in a group of 40` LESS THAN 365

§§ `X4 — a disappearance cannot be claimed in time`

-- An insured vanishes in an accident on 1 March 2026 (the day of the last news). Def 34
-- lets a court declare them missing no earlier than 1 March 2028. Part VII wants the accident
-- documents by 1 March 2027 (12 months), the accident notice within 120 days, and any claim
-- file within a year of the last treatment. The declaration VI.11 needs (fork F32) arrives
-- a year after the documents were due.
#ASSERT `the earliest day a court may declare the person missing, given` (`the day of the last news` (YMD 2026 3 1)) EQUALS YMD 2028 3 1
#ASSERT `the earliest day a court may declare the person missing, given` (`the day of the last news` (YMD 2026 3 1)) GREATER THAN `add months` (YMD 2026 3 1) 12

§§ `X9 — a charity race: spared by definition 62, caught by exclusion 28`

#ASSERT NOT `a dangerous sport` `a charity race`
#ASSERT NOT `the claim is covered` (`the employee's claim for` (`an accident on` (YMD 2026 6 1) `with` (LIST `taking part in an activity` `a charity race` FALSE FALSE TRUE)) `on` `Benefit 1` `for` (`death` FALSE) `on` (YMD 2026 6 1))

§§ `X10 — occupational diseases the occupational disease extension lists and the exclusions take back`

GIVEN occupational IS AN `An occupational disease`
      circumstance IS A `A circumstance`
GIVETH A `A claim`
`an occupational claim for` occupational `with` circumstance MEANS
    `a claim under` (`a 2026 contract for` 60 `employees and` 120 `persons with` `every extension`) `by` `the employee`
        `for` (`an event built from` `an illness` (YMD 2026 6 1) TRUE FALSE `another illness or injury` (YMD 2026 6 1) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING (LIST circumstance) (JUST occupational) TRUE)
        `on` `Benefit 6` `for` (`medical expenses` (`an outpatient visit on` (YMD 2026 6 1)) EMPTY) `on` (YMD 2026 6 1)

-- VI.8 item (13), occupational tuberculosis: IV.A.9 excludes pulmonary tuberculosis.
#ASSERT `an occupational disease within VI.8` (`a 2026 contract for` 60 `employees and` 120 `persons with` `every extension`) ((`an occupational claim for` `occupational tuberculosis` `with` `pulmonary tuberculosis`)'s `the event`)
#ASSERT NOT `the claim is covered` (`an occupational claim for` `occupational tuberculosis` `with` `pulmonary tuberculosis`)
-- VI.8 item (7), X-ray and radiation sickness: IV.A.7 excludes radioactive contamination.
#ASSERT NOT `the claim is covered` (`an occupational claim for` `X-ray and radiation sickness` `with` `radioactive contamination`)

§§ `X11 — the table pays the loss of one foot at 100% (item 5) and at 40-50% (item 30)`

-- Item 5 of section II lists "mất một cánh tay hoặc một bàn chân" (losing an arm OR a foot)
-- among the 100% injuries; item 30 lists losing a foot at 40-50%. On a sum insured of
-- 100.000.000 the two rows pay 100.000.000 and 40.000.000 for the same foot.
#ASSERT `the amount under the table on` 100000000 `for` (LIST `a listed injury` 5 1 `normal healing, without infection` FALSE NOTHING) EQUALS 100000000
#ASSERT `the amount under the table on` 100000000 `for` (LIST `a listed injury` 30 1 `normal healing, without infection` FALSE NOTHING) EQUALS 40000000

§§ `X16 — the premium payment warranty: a condition precedent that preserves liability`

-- Premium never paid; an accident on 10 February 2026, inside the 60 days. On fork F26 the
-- claim is covered; on the clause's own "condition precedent" it is not.
#ASSERT `the claim is covered` (`a claim built from` (`a 2026 contract for` 60 `employees and` 120 `persons with` `every extension`) `the employee` (`an accident on` (YMD 2026 2 10) `with` EMPTY) `Benefit 1` (`death` FALSE) (YMD 2026 2 10) 0 NOTHING FALSE NOTHING NOTHING FALSE (`a file submitted on` (YMD 2026 2 10)))

§§ `X18 — extensions that add nothing`

-- An unprovoked assault is covered under the plain contract, without VI.10; a riot is not
-- excluded, without VI.5.
#ASSERT `the claim is covered` (`the employee's claim for` (`an accident on` (YMD 2026 6 1) `with` (LIST `an attempted murder or an unprovoked assault`)) `on` `Benefit 1` `for` (`death` FALSE) `on` (YMD 2026 6 1))
#ASSERT `the claim is covered` (`the employee's claim for` (`an accident on` (YMD 2026 6 1) `with` (LIST `a riot or civil commotion`)) `on` `Benefit 1` `for` (`death` FALSE) `on` (YMD 2026 6 1))

§§ `X19 — prenatal checks: covered, but under no benefit and no limit`

#ASSERT REFUSED `the amount payable on` (`a claim under` (`a 2026 contract for` 60 `employees and` 120 `persons with` `every extension`) `by` (`a new member` `a spouse` `born on` (YMD 1995 1 1)) `for` (`an event of kind` `a pregnancy, for routine prenatal care` `on` (YMD 2026 5 1)) `on` `Benefit 6` `for` (`medical expenses` (`an outpatient visit on` (YMD 2026 5 1)) (LIST `an item of` `a prenatal check-up or ultrasound` `for` 500000 `on` (YMD 2026 5 1))) `on` (YMD 2026 5 1)) BECAUSE "VI.12 names no benefit or limit for prenatal checks"

§§ `X23 — an overnight admission of less than 24 hours is not a "hospital stay"`

-- Admitted at 8 pm, discharged at 7 am (11 hours, overnight): inpatient treatment by def 25,
-- but not "nằm viện" by def 35 (more than 24 continuous hours), nor day treatment (no
-- overnight stay). Benefit 4 pays no room charge for it.
GIVETH A `A claim`
`an 11-hour overnight claim` MEANS
    `the employee's claim for` (`an illness from` (YMD 2026 6 1) `diagnosed as` `another illness or injury` `with` EMPTY) `on` `Benefit 4`
        `for` (`medical expenses` (`a treatment built from` `inpatient treatment` (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 6 2) TRUE TRUE 11 `a hospital` `a licensed doctor` FALSE)
                  (LIST `an item of` (`room and board` 1) `for` 800000 `on` (YMD 2026 6 1)))
        `on` (YMD 2026 6 1)

#ASSERT `counts as inpatient treatment` (`a treatment built from` `inpatient treatment` (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 6 2) TRUE TRUE 11 `a hospital` `a licensed doctor` FALSE)
#ASSERT `the claim is covered` `an 11-hour overnight claim`
#ASSERT `the amount payable on` `an 11-hour overnight claim` EQUALS 0

§§ `X24 — Benefit 2 does not list a consultation fee for an accident treated as an outpatient`

#ASSERT `the amount payable on` (`the employee's claim for` (`an accident on` (YMD 2026 6 1) `with` EMPTY) `on` `Benefit 2` `for` (`medical expenses` (`an outpatient visit on` (YMD 2026 6 1)) (LIST `an item of` `a consultation` `for` 300000 `on` (YMD 2026 6 1))) `on` (YMD 2026 6 1)) EQUALS 0

§§ `X25 — Benefit 1's two-year tail outruns Part VII's twelve months`

-- An accident on 1 December 2026, notified on 5 December; death on 30 November 2028, inside
-- III.6's two years, so the benefit is payable. The death certificate cannot be sent before
-- the death, which is after Part VII's 12 months from the accident: the claim falls to be
-- refused in part or whole, by an amount the document does not state.
GIVETH A `A claim`
`a death 23 months after an accident` MEANS
    `a claim built from` `the plain contract` `the employee` (`an accident on` (YMD 2026 12 1) `with` EMPTY) `Benefit 1` (`death` FALSE) (YMD 2028 11 30)
        0 NOTHING FALSE (JUST (YMD 2026 1 1)) NOTHING FALSE
        (`The claim file` WITH
            `through the direct billing network`                    IS FALSE
            `kind of accident`                                      IS JUST `an accident in daily life`
            `a serious traffic accident, fatal or involving a third party` IS FALSE
            `date the claim file was submitted`                     IS YMD 2028 12 5
            `date the accident was notified in writing`             IS JUST (YMD 2026 12 5)
            `date the documents were sent`                          IS YMD 2028 12 5
            `date supplementary documents were requested`           IS NOTHING
            `date supplementary documents were submitted`           IS NOTHING
            `force majeure`                                         IS FALSE
            `an invoice lumps several kinds of cost together`       IS FALSE
            `documents supplied`                                    IS EMPTY)

#ASSERT `the amount payable on` `a death 23 months after an accident` EQUALS 100000000
#ASSERT REFUSED `the amount PTI must pay on` `a death 23 months after an accident` BECAUSE "late accident documents are refused in part or in whole, and the document does not say how much"

